# Force LF line endings for text files regardless of a contributor's local
# core.autocrlf setting. Without this, a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true converts every source file to CRLF on disk; the git
# blobs themselves stay LF-only, but `docker build` COPYs the working-tree
# bytes (CRLF) into the image, and eslint's prettier/prettier rule then
# reports thousands of `Delete \r` errors that have nothing to do with the
# actual code (verified during the 2026-09 audit pass: after normalizing to
# LF, exactly one real lint issue remained, unrelated to line endings).
* text=auto eol=lf
